{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795086209,"nonce":"l4PJN4iUpDZfE/mSQpjY+7FUcj8=","title":"Deliver notifications shared by statically linked libraries to every matching inbox","message":"hxn-assets graph verification exposed a core delivery error. Multiple statically linked adapters may resolve to the same hxn-future outbox. Each generated Haxe inbox currently removes all queued IDs but dispatches only its own watchers, so one library can consume another library’s completion notification. Android hxcpp can stall after a file preference request followed by concurrent graph queries. Add a deterministic shared-queue Haxe regression and dispatch queued IDs to matching watchers across registered inboxes; each watcher checks its own readiness, so independently allocated IDs remain safe. Validate native, CPPIA, Ash and both browser backends, and publish the core patch before the embedded graph release.","files":null}]}